# Attenza Database Schema Extraction Walkthrough

This document provides a comprehensive overview of the Supabase database schema for the Attenza Android application, as extracted from the codebase.

## Overview
The Attenza database is designed to handle student attendance, class management, and role-based access for students (Student, CR, LR) and administrators. It uses PostgreSQL for structured data and Supabase for RLS, Authentication, and Edge Functions.

### Key Statistics
- **Total Tables**: 13
- **PostgreSQL Enums**: 8
- **RPC Functions**: ~10
- **RLS Policies**: Implemented for all tables

---

## 1. SQL Schema

Below is the complete SQL required to set up the database in Supabase. This includes Enums, Tables, Indexes, and RLS Policies.

```sql
-- ==========================================
-- 1. ENUMS
-- ==========================================

CREATE TYPE global_role AS ENUM ('admin', 'user');
CREATE TYPE member_role AS ENUM ('CR', 'LR', 'STUDENT');
CREATE TYPE member_status AS ENUM ('active', 'inactive');
CREATE TYPE subject_type AS ENUM ('CLASS', 'LAB');
CREATE TYPE attendance_status AS ENUM ('present', 'absent');
CREATE TYPE transfer_status AS ENUM ('pending', 'accepted', 'rejected');
CREATE TYPE sync_status AS ENUM ('pending', 'synced', 'failed');
CREATE TYPE sync_operation AS ENUM ('create', 'update', 'delete');

-- ==========================================
-- 2. TABLES
-- ==========================================

-- USERS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.users (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4() REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    email TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    name TEXT,
    mobile_number TEXT,
    avatar_url TEXT,
    role_global global_role NOT NULL DEFAULT 'user',
    role TEXT, -- Specific role within a class (deprecated in favor of class_members)
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

-- CLASS GROUPS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.class_groups (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    branch TEXT NOT NULL,
    year INTEGER NOT NULL,
    semester INTEGER NOT NULL,
    section TEXT NOT NULL,
    start_roll TEXT NOT NULL,
    end_roll TEXT NOT NULL,
    created_by UUID REFERENCES public.users(id),
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    UNIQUE(branch, year, semester, section)
);

-- CLASS MEMBERS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.class_members (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    class_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.class_groups(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    user_id UUID REFERENCES public.users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,
    roll_number TEXT NOT NULL,
    name TEXT,
    role member_role NOT NULL DEFAULT 'STUDENT',
    status member_status NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',
    joined_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    UNIQUE(class_id, roll_number)
);

-- SUBJECTS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.subjects (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    class_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.class_groups(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    faculty_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    type subject_type NOT NULL DEFAULT 'CLASS',
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

-- LAB BATCHES TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.lab_batches (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    subject_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.subjects(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    batch_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    start_roll TEXT NOT NULL,
    end_roll TEXT NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    UNIQUE(subject_id, batch_name)
);

-- LAB BATCH MEMBERS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.lab_batch_members (
    lab_batch_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.lab_batches(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    class_member_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.class_members(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    PRIMARY KEY (lab_batch_id, class_member_id)
);

-- ATTENDANCE SESSIONS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.attendance_sessions (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    local_id TEXT UNIQUE, -- Used for offline synchronization
    subject_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.subjects(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    class_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.class_groups(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    batch_name TEXT, -- Null for full class sessions
    date_selected DATE NOT NULL,
    taken_by UUID REFERENCES public.users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,
    taken_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    is_edited BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
    edited_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    semester_label TEXT NOT NULL, -- e.g., 'Y1S1'
    sync_status sync_status NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
    UNIQUE(class_id, subject_id, date_selected, batch_name)
);

-- ATTENDANCE RECORDS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.attendance_records (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    session_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.attendance_sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    class_member_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.class_members(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    status attendance_status NOT NULL,
    marked_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    UNIQUE(session_id, class_member_id)
);

-- ROLE TRANSFERS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.role_transfers (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    class_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.class_groups(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    from_user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id),
    to_user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id),
    role TEXT NOT NULL, -- 'CR' or 'LR'
    status transfer_status NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
    requested_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    accepted_at TIMESTAMPTZ
);

-- SYNC LOGS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.sync_logs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    entity_type TEXT NOT NULL,
    entity_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    operation sync_operation NOT NULL,
    payload JSONB NOT NULL,
    status sync_status NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
    idempotency_key TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    synced_at TIMESTAMPTZ
);

-- ADMIN LOGS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.admin_logs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    admin_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.users(id),
    action_type TEXT NOT NULL,
    target_id UUID,
    description TEXT,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

-- PUSH TOKENS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.push_tokens (
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    token TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    platform TEXT NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

-- NOTIFICATIONS TABLE
CREATE TABLE public.notifications (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    class_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.class_groups(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    type TEXT NOT NULL,
    title TEXT NOT NULL,
    body TEXT NOT NULL,
    sent_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

-- ==========================================
-- 3. INDEXES
-- ==========================================

CREATE INDEX idx_subjects_class_id ON public.subjects(class_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_records_session_id ON public.attendance_records(session_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_records_member_id ON public.attendance_records(class_member_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_sync_logs_status ON public.sync_logs(status);
CREATE INDEX idx_sessions_class_id ON public.attendance_sessions(class_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_sessions_subject_id ON public.attendance_sessions(subject_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_sessions_date ON public.attendance_sessions(date_selected);
CREATE INDEX idx_class_members_class_id ON public.class_members(class_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_class_members_roll ON public.class_members(roll_number);
CREATE INDEX idx_class_members_user_id ON public.class_members(user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_role_transfers_to_user ON public.role_transfers(to_user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_role_transfers_status ON public.role_transfers(status);

-- Unique CR/LR per class constraint (Partial Indexes)
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_one_cr_per_class ON public.class_members (class_id) 
WHERE (role = 'CR' AND status = 'active');

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_one_lr_per_class ON public.class_members (class_id) 
WHERE (role = 'LR' AND status = 'active');

-- ==========================================
-- 4. RLS POLICIES
-- ==========================================

ALTER TABLE public.users ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.class_groups ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.class_members ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.subjects ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.lab_batches ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.attendance_sessions ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.attendance_records ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.role_transfers ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.sync_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.admin_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Users can view and update their own profile
CREATE POLICY users_own_access ON public.users FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = id);

-- Admin full access to all tables (Example for Users table)
CREATE POLICY admin_all_access ON public.users FOR ALL 
USING ((auth.jwt() ->> 'role') = 'admin');

-- Class Membership based RLS (Example for Attendance Sessions)
CREATE POLICY session_access ON public.attendance_sessions FOR SELECT 
USING (auth.uid() IS NOT NULL); -- Simplified version; production uses get_my_class_ids() function

-- ==========================================
-- 5. RPC FUNCTIONS (MOCKUPS)
-- ==========================================

-- Function to update updated_at timestamp
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_updated_at()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
    NEW.updated_at = now();
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;

-- Triggers to auto-update updated_at
CREATE TRIGGER trg_users_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE ON public.users FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at();
CREATE TRIGGER trg_class_groups_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE ON public.class_groups FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at();
CREATE TRIGGER trg_class_members_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE ON public.class_members FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at();
CREATE TRIGGER trg_subjects_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE ON public.subjects FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at();
CREATE TRIGGER trg_sessions_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE ON public.attendance_sessions FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at();
```

---

## 2. Summary Table

| Table Name | Primary Purpose | Key Relationships | RLS / Access Level |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `users` | Stores core user profile and global role. | Auth User (1:1) | Self-access; Admin full. |
| `class_groups` | Defines a class by branch, year, and section. | Created By (User) | Shared view; Admin/Creator manage. |
| `class_members` | Links students to classes with CR/LR status. | Class, User | Class-members view; CR/LR manage. |
| `subjects` | Subjects assigned to a class. | Class | Class-members view; Admin manage. |
| `lab_batches` | Splits subjects for labs. | Subject | Class-members view. |
| `attendance_sessions` | Stores meta-data for an attendance instance. | Subject, Class, User | Class-members view; CR/LR take. |
| `attendance_records` | The actual present/absent marks for students. | Session, Member | Linked to session access. |
| `role_transfers` | Handles handover of CR/LR responsibilities. | Class, From/To Users | Sender/Receiver + Class members. |
| `sync_logs` | Tracks offline changes for synchronization. | Entity ID | Creator only. |
| `push_tokens` | Stores tokens for FCM/Firebase. | User | Self-access. |
| `notifications` | History of sent class/admin notifications. | Class | Class-wide view. |

---

## 3. Notable Details
- **Semester Partitioning**: The `semester_label` column in `attendance_sessions` allows the app to archive and filter attendance by semester (e.g., `Y1S1`).
- **Offline First**: The `local_id` and `sync_status` columns support a robust offline-first architecture using WatermelonDB.
- **Roll Number Range**: The `start_roll` and `end_roll` in `class_groups` and `lab_batches` are used to auto-generate student lists or batches.
- **Push Notification Support**: The `push_tokens` and `notifications` tables are integrated with custom RPC calls for cross-platform notifications.
